From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luma: keep the notification rules last in the sheets and drop
 stale icon resources

The Studio Quick Options rules were appended after the notification-owned
suffix of gnome-shell-dark, -light and -high-contrast.css, so the build's
verify-generated.sh check failed; they now sit in front of the suffix,
unchanged. The Studio glyphs moved to the installed hicolor theme, but the
icon resource still listed them, so glib-compile-resources failed; the
stale resource entries are dropped (the glyphs load from the theme).

diff --git a/data/gnome-shell-icons.gresource.xml b/data/gnome-shell-icons.gresource.xml
index d98f396..31bef1a 100644
--- a/data/gnome-shell-icons.gresource.xml
+++ b/data/gnome-shell-icons.gresource.xml
@@ -70,25 +70,6 @@
     <file preprocess="xml-stripblanks">scalable/status/switch-off-symbolic.svg</file>
     <file preprocess="xml-stripblanks">scalable/status/switch-on-symbolic.svg</file>
     <file preprocess="xml-stripblanks">scalable/status/wellbeing-symbolic.svg</file>
-    <file preprocess="xml-stripblanks">scalable/status/luma-sun-symbolic.svg</file>
-    <file preprocess="xml-stripblanks">scalable/status/luma-sun-moon-symbolic.svg</file>
